title: "Fewer planned US generators now start in the month they were due"
abstract: "Of generators that EIA-860M listed as planned for the next month, the share operating in that month fell from 0.469 in 2016-2019 to 0.349 in 2022-2025. About 79% of the fall happened inside technologies, led by solar and batteries. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
